From 5587483d502544e00af7cc97e25dc3cc66e06a83 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: z060142 <z060142@yahoo.com.tw>
Date: Thu, 27 Aug 2026 13:24:32 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 56/57] fix: the wave glare moves to half resolution, its own
 layer and a pre-blurred source

The square core and the visible blocks around every lamp were not windowing
faults, and the inner/outer windows of the last round did not cure them (as
that round's own comment predicted). Two rasterization faults, both cured by
the same move:

  * SOURCE grid. A lamp clears the threshold over a ~3x3 block of quarter-res
    texels, each of which spawns its own sprite. The sum of nine offset copies
    of a radially symmetric pattern has the BLOCK's square as its centre,
    whatever the pupil was.
  * DEPOSIT grid. A quarter-res deposit is bilinearly magnified 4x onto the
    pattern's 1/u^2 slope, which crosses a whole texel in almost nothing -
    4x4 native blocks.

Half resolution halves both in each axis, and a separable 5-tap Gaussian
pre-blur (sigma ~ 1 half-res texel, weights normalised so the total excess is
preserved) turns what is left of the source block into a round blob. The blur
is physics, not smoothing: it is the convolution of the pattern with the
source's own extent.

Renderer:
  - threshold the half-res HDR downsample ($HDRTarget 1/2a, still intact at
    this point in the frame) into a half-res scratch RT, 1:1 instead of the
    old 2:1 minification; blur H; blur V.
  - deposit into $DiffractionLayer, a half-res RGBA16F layer owned by the
    bloom stage, acquired/released/resized like the halation targets and
    cleared per frame the pass runs.
  - composite it into the HDR target with an additive bilinear fullscreen
    blit from CBloomStage::ExecuteDiffractionComposite(), called by the
    pipeline right before the DOF's ghost composite - after every glare
    threshold has been taken, so the pattern cannot halate or streak off
    itself, exactly as with the ghosts.
  - sprite grid, pitch, sprite radius, 1/s^2 norm and the inner window (now
    4 half-res px = the same 8 native) all in half-res px.

Energy: because the layer no longer travels through $HDRFinalBloom, the
1 / fBloomCompositeWeight factor is REMOVED. On screen the deposit is
unchanged - deposit * (1/w) * w became deposit - and the resolution move is
neutral too, since the pitch doubles (per-pixel deposit quartered) while the
sprite covers four times as many pixels.

Debug modes 1-3 all still work; mode 3's panel now reads the half-res
thresholded and pre-blurred source, which is what the sprite grid walks. The
log prints the sprite radius in half-res and native px: sprites are 2x wider
and there are 4x as many candidate cells, so Streak Reach is the cost dial.

New shader techniques HDRDiffractionSourceBlur and HDRDiffractionComposite.
Spec, README and ConsoleReference updated.

